<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 04:31:12 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Trump calls renewed Ukraine attacks on Russian oil refineries 'a disgrace'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-live-trump-calls-renewed-ukraine-attacks-on-russian-oil-refineries-a-disgrace</link><description>
US President Donald Trump called Ukraine's renewed strikes on Russian oil refineries a "disgrace" after Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky rejected his calls for an "energy ceasefire." Zelensky sought support from European allies earlier that day in Brussels on the sidelines of an EU summit. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/72deca9a-c900-11f1-a741-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288658174476.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/72deca9a-c900-11f1-a741-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288658174476.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ec95e172-c903-11f1-b093-3b96d215f849</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 01:50:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/72deca9a-c900-11f1-a741-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288658174476.jpg">© Julia Demaree Nikhinson, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>19 injured as minibus crashes into train at Channel Tunnel entrance</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-19-injured-as-minibus-crashes-into-train-at-channel-tunnel-entrance</link><description>
Nineteen people were injured Thursday when a minibus carrying truck drivers crashed into a vehicle shuttle train at the French entrance to the Channel Tunnel near Calais, forcing a 90-minute suspension of shuttle services. Two people were hospitalised with serious but non-life-threatening injuries, French authorities said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a8daece-71cc-11f0-9526-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-397M8WK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a8daece-71cc-11f0-9526-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-397M8WK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f99b5af8-c8fb-11f1-b305-c7c144120c8c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:53:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a8daece-71cc-11f0-9526-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-397M8WK.jpg">© Sameer Al-Doumy, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>France and Germany agree to ease EU car emissions rules in new deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-france-and-germany-agree-to-ease-eu-car-emissions-rules-in-new-deal</link><description>
France and Germany have backed looser EU emissions rules for carmakers and agreed to include Britain in a “made in Europe” scheme, in a provisional deal reached Thursday that could reshape the bloc’s automotive and climate policies.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af286218-c8e7-11f1-8247-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26270718148994.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af286218-c8e7-11f1-8247-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26270718148994.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fd324f7c-c8f2-11f1-a500-2b19cb1aea8f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:48:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af286218-c8e7-11f1-8247-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26270718148994.jpg">© Michael Sohn, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky rallies European allies as US support for Ukraine wanes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-zelensky-rallies-european-allies-as-us-support-for-ukraine-wanes</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky sought European backing Thursday after vowing to resume strikes on Russian oil refineries despite US President Donald Trump’s demands, as tensions with Washington escalated over sanctions, energy infrastructure attacks and restrictions on satellite communications.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28bbd5dc-c8d5-11f1-aec7-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/80c62e6fc13f8d6a5641fe9e16da5b4e0ca12147.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28bbd5dc-c8d5-11f1-aec7-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/80c62e6fc13f8d6a5641fe9e16da5b4e0ca12147.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fd8e39fa-c8ec-11f1-a26b-7beb10019f07</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:06:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28bbd5dc-c8d5-11f1-aec7-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/80c62e6fc13f8d6a5641fe9e16da5b4e0ca12147.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'It is clear that sooner or later we will have European casualties', Romanian MEP</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/it-is-clear-that-sooner-or-later-we-will-have-european-casualties-romanian-mep</link><description>
Rescuers searched on Thursday for seven missing sailors after drones struck two chemical tankers near Romania's Black Sea coast, setting them ablaze and raising fresh security concerns along a vital shipping route used by Ukraine. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Europe editor Armen Georgian, Nicolae Stefanuta, Romanian MEP and Co-Chair of the Group of the Greens, says that the Danube delta region is facing a more intense threat from Russia than Baltic States and that "it is clear that sooner or later we will have European casualties".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc7eaac2-c8d2-11f1-b063-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-211432-211932-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc7eaac2-c8d2-11f1-b063-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-211432-211932-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c1b2e1d4-c8d2-11f1-925f-cb689c3210d5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:03:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Donald Trump 'openly financing Russia's war with Ukraine', Nobel peace laureate says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-openly-financing-russia-s-war-with-ukraine-nobel-peace-laureate-says</link><description>
Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Nobel Peace laureate Oleksandra Matviichuk, Director of the Centre for Civil Liberties, says that with the diesel-supply deal with Moscow Donald Trump "is openly financing this war, by lifting sanctions is providing Russia with opportunities to earn more money" adding that "extra money will be converted in rockets and drones and additional deaths among the civilian population".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dc8c71c-c8cf-11f1-b194-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-210633-211324-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dc8c71c-c8cf-11f1-b194-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-210633-211324-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">72e458d8-c8cf-11f1-b211-61fe1cac82d8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:48:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Seven missing off Romania after latest Black Sea drone attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/seven-missing-off-romania-after-latest-black-sea-drone-attacks</link><description>
Romania reported seven people missing on Thursday after two drone attacks on ships in the Black Sea, where several vessels have been hit recently in suspected fallout from the Ukraine war. The attacks are the latest in a series off the coast of Romania and neighbouring Bulgaria in recent weeks. FRANCE 24's Eliza Herbert reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d4a8504-c8c9-11f1-bf1b-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-203417-203608-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d4a8504-c8c9-11f1-bf1b-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-203417-203608-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">96ab9714-c8c9-11f1-8c3c-27acdd5cac97</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:04:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Albania's leader defies calls to resign as student protesters rampage in capital</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/albania-s-leader-defies-calls-to-resign-as-student-protesters-rampage-in-capital</link><description>
​Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama on Thursday rejected calls to resign as thousands of student-led protesters smashed windows and fought running battles with riot police firing water cannon and tear gas in the capital. The demonstrators accuse officials of corruption and neglecting education and say they are angry about the sale of parts of Albania's southern coastline to a luxury resort development backed ​by US President ‌Donald Trump's son-in-law Jared Kushner. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/281c8484-c8c9-11f1-8ffe-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-200906-201102-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/281c8484-c8c9-11f1-8ffe-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-200906-201102-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">38d566e2-c8c9-11f1-b983-7f8e2f52719a</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:02:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Will Trump really pull the plug? Starlink restored but Ukraine's fate still uncertain</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261015-will-trump-really-pull-the-plug-starlink-restored-but-ukraine-s-fate-still-uncertain</link><description>
Can a flick of a switch really be enough for Donald Trump and Elon Musk to end Ukraine's hopes of holding out against Russia? With Kyiv already reeling from daily strikes by Russia's new motor-powered drones, the United States decision to slow SpaceX Starlink service felt immediately Wednesday when air raid warnings failed.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0be3d78c-c8c3-11f1-936e-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-15T074057Z-616239413-RC233OAF2BZE-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-DONETSK-REGION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0be3d78c-c8c3-11f1-936e-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-15T074057Z-616239413-RC233OAF2BZE-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-DONETSK-REGION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b90d2078-c8c1-11f1-b4e2-b7b3e4e3c9a4</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:38:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Why have US-Ukraine relations soured ahead of the midterms?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-why-have-us-ukraine-relations-soured-ahead-of-the-midterms</link><description>
Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky said he felt “betrayed” on Wednesday after access was seemingly restricted to US intelligence and Space X satellite services, raising new questions about US commitment to Ukraine. With Trump under pressure over rising fuel prices, is the White House hoping criticism of Kyiv can help shift the blame? 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b15f302e-c8ac-11f1-a90d-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26281714511676.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b15f302e-c8ac-11f1-a90d-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26281714511676.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d58215b2-c8ab-11f1-95cb-9d4b1f97111e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:54:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b15f302e-c8ac-11f1-a90d-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26281714511676.jpg">© Julia Demaree Nikhinson, AP</source><dc:creator>Joanna YORK</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'We're done': Ukraine resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries as 'only leverage' for peace talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-we-re-done-ukraine-resumes-strikes-on-russian-oil-refineries-as-only-leverage-for-peace-talks-1</link><description>
Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative, LIVE from Kyiv. As Zelensky declares Ukraine "done" with Trump's self-declared energy ceasefire and resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries, Zalmayev warns: "When you talk about the energy ceasefire, it presupposes two to be able to tango and to dance this dance." He challenges the legitimacy of Trump's unilateral announcement, made without agreement between Moscow and Kyiv, as Russia continues attacking Ukraine's energy infrastructure. Yet he cautions that Zelensky may need tactical restraint to preserve vital US support. Zalmayev also examines Western sanctions, frozen Russian assets, and Washington's pursuit of economic normalization with Moscow without meaningful Russian concessions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58af4524-c8af-11f1-8d33-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-130211-131029-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58af4524-c8af-11f1-8d33-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-130211-131029-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a36ed962-c8af-11f1-bc01-231790081c82</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:14:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>NATO to address drone attacks in the Black Sea after seven missing off Romania</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-seven-missing-off-romania-after-latest-black-sea-drone-attacks</link><description>
NATO will put drone strikes in the Black Sea on its agenda at a meeting next week, officials said Thursday, following two new attacks and the disappearance of seven people. Incidents involving civilian vessels in the Black Sea have been on the rise off the coasts of Bulgaria and Romania in a suspected spillover from Russia’s war in Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e42d5b20-c8a7-11f1-a87e-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/9e825dda6ecaf41ed8fa636033ec60663423d630.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e42d5b20-c8a7-11f1-a87e-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/9e825dda6ecaf41ed8fa636033ec60663423d630.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">45d51de6-c89d-11f1-9236-07b36ca1617f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:35:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e42d5b20-c8a7-11f1-a87e-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/9e825dda6ecaf41ed8fa636033ec60663423d630.jpg">© Handout from Ministry of Interior Bulgaria via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Student protests spread in Albania as demonstrators call for PM resignation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-student-protests-escalate-in-albania-as-demonstrators-call-for-pm-resignation</link><description>
Clashes broke out between demonstrators and police for the third consecutive day on Thursday in Albania, with Prime Minister Edi Rama condemning the “chaos” that caused damage to government buildings. Thousands of protesters are calling for Rama's resignation and better studying conditions for Albanian students.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c62f1866-c893-11f1-bbdd-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/c5d39ddd12d0832bc704ebd4b58a7ca0b7ebbee6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c62f1866-c893-11f1-bbdd-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/c5d39ddd12d0832bc704ebd4b58a7ca0b7ebbee6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c70462d2-c893-11f1-9ecb-4d9714b03f50</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:27:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c62f1866-c893-11f1-bbdd-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/c5d39ddd12d0832bc704ebd4b58a7ca0b7ebbee6.jpg">© Adnan Beci, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia detains independent outlet Novaya Gazeta editor Sergei Sokolov</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-russia-detains-novaya-gazeta-editor-in-chief-sergei-sokolov-after-home-search</link><description>
Sergei Sokolov, the editor-in-chief of Russia's independent newspaper Novaya Gazeta, was detained and taken for questioning on Thursday after authorities searched his home, the newspaper said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8c2f0c-c88b-11f1-8592-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3D79KE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8c2f0c-c88b-11f1-8592-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3D79KE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f0ab8140-c88b-11f1-9849-0fbb85ce41e0</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:39:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd8c2f0c-c88b-11f1-8592-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3D79KE.jpg">© Igor Ivanko, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>'American abandonment' threatens Ukraine's civilians in war against Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261015-american-abandonment-threatens-ukraine-s-civilians-in-war-against-russia</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, October 15: First, reported Starlink disruptions in Ukraine make the European front pages. Next, US papers go into more detail about the situation. Also, an unusual alliance forms in Germany between far-right and far-left parties. Meanwhile, the winners of the Wildlife Photographer of the Year awards have been announced. Finally, Finland flaunts its smelly islands.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ee85026-c885-11f1-9705-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5116b1de.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ee85026-c885-11f1-9705-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5116b1de.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">804e3c42-c865-11f1-bc3e-3114adfafbf4</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:09:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Emily BOYLE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>War in Ukraine: Kyiv residents decry shortage of bomb shelters</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261015-war-in-ukraine-kyiv-residents-decry-shortage-of-bomb-shelters</link><description>
Kyiv's mayor, Vitaly Klitschko, has advised those residents who can "temporarily relocate" for the winter to do so. That advice has been met with derision at best from many residents, who say his administration is responsible for failing to better prepare the Ukrainian capital for Russian attacks. In particular, they complain of a severe shortage of adequate bomb shelters.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ff98ea6-c876-11f1-99ac-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5eb8f3a5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ff98ea6-c876-11f1-99ac-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5eb8f3a5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">911c1920-c7cc-11f1-8e80-b783564a2256</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:50:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gulliver CRAGG</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>EU leaders head into high-stakes budget battle as elections loom</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/eu-leaders-head-into-high-stakes-budget-battle-as-elections-loom</link><description>
EU leaders head to a summit on Thursday seeking a deal on the bloc’s nearly €2 trillion budget for 2028-2034 by Christmas amid deep divisions over spending and fears that upcoming elections, particularly in France, could strengthen eurosceptic forces.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aa7737e-c83c-11f1-af7d-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/90bd5f4c90f09eb957948de43a7ce1797745125f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aa7737e-c83c-11f1-af7d-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/90bd5f4c90f09eb957948de43a7ce1797745125f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cdfb3e8e-c85d-11f1-8339-0d5a9df05665</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:03:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>France 'can no longer finance' Ukraine, far-right presidential frontrunner Le Pen says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-france-can-no-longer-finance-ukraine-far-right-candidate-marine-le-pen-says</link><description>
Far-right leader and presidential candidate Marine Le Pen said on Wednesday that France could no longer afford to fund Ukraine, citing the country's high deficit and weak economic growth.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/212d5b6c-c85b-11f1-910c-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3B329N.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/212d5b6c-c85b-11f1-910c-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3B329N.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8c9d7838-c85a-11f1-8246-25553aadac69</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:49:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/212d5b6c-c85b-11f1-910c-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3B329N.jpg">© Nicolas Tucas, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky meets NATO chief and EU leaders in push to apply 'real pressure' on Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-ukraine-live-romania-probes-possible-drone-attack-on-tanker</link><description>
